# Implementation debugging log

When an **implementation** session enters a debugging loop (repeated hypothesis → change → rebuild/boot or test → result), create a timestamped log in that component’s specs folder **before** the second iteration. Do not rely on chat alone.

```text
tavera/specs/<component>/debugging-YYYY-MM-DD.md
```

`<component>` matches the module folder already used for specs and `open-items.md` (for example `amd64-logical-processors`). Date is the day the loop started (UTC or local calendar date; keep one convention for the file).

If a second distinct loop starts on the same day for the same component, add a suffix: `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD-2.md`, then `-3`, and so on. Do not overwrite an earlier loop’s file.

## What counts as a debugging loop

- More than one rebuild/boot or targeted test while chasing the same fault
- A series of temporary diagnostics (breadcrumbs, affinity pins, park loops) aimed at one failure

A single failed boot with an immediate correct fix is not enough to require the file. Opening the file on the first failed check is fine when a loop is clearly starting.

## File contents

Use the same HTML comment header block other files under `tavera/specs/<component>/` use. Then record, in order:

1. Harness (guest, QEMU flags, build command, image)
2. Each cycle: hypothesis → change (paths) → evidence (log under `sources/debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/` or marker) → result
3. What remains open and the next check

Update the same file in the same turn as each new cycle. Do not paste large log bodies.

In the same turn, copy every cited `output/` file that still exists into
**both** `tavera/specs/<component>/sources/debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/` and the
private capture-log mirror, then cite the **public** `sources/…` path in this
debugging file, per [tavera-specs-sources.mdc](tavera-specs-sources.mdc).
Do **not** name `capture-log` in the public debugging file. When a cited
path is already gone from `output/` and from `sources/`, tell Ryan and note
“proof missing” only in the private archive `README.md`.

```text
Right: tavera/specs/amd64-logical-processors/debugging-2026-11-18.md started when AP join failed; each boot logged
Right: cite tavera/specs/…/sources/debugging-2026-11-18/boot-m32-….log; also mirror under capture-log privately
Wrong: ten QEMU boots with notes only in chat
Wrong: tavera/specs/debugging.md (no component folder, no date)
Wrong: overwriting yesterday’s debugging-*.md for a new fault
Wrong: naming capture-log in the public debugging file
Wrong: citing output/… after the file was copied into sources/
Wrong: public sources/ copy with no private capture-log mirror
```

This rule does not replace `open-items.md`. Spec gaps still go there. The debugging file is the implementer’s running fault trail.
